KDOS-cursors is a KDOS-specific derivative of the Bibata cursor theme.

  Upstream:  Bibata_Cursor — https://github.com/ful1e5/Bibata_Cursor
  Variant:   Bibata-Modern-Ice, release v2.0.7 (recorded in art/UPSTREAM)
  Licence:   GNU General Public License v3.0 — the upstream repository holds
             the full licence text and the original SVG sources

The artwork in art/ is NOT upstream's release as shipped. It is a pruned,
vendored subset produced by vendor.py, and the theme built from it is
recoloured by gencursors.py. Specifically:

  * Only the 32 shapes KDOS actually needs are kept. Upstream's X11 relics
    (pirate/X_cursor, dotbox, draped box, target, corner tees and angles,
    scrollbar arrows, draft, cross variants, colour picker) are dropped.
  * Only five sizes are kept — 24, 32, 48, 64, 96 — out of upstream's fourteen.
  * The two animated shapes are decimated from 54 frames to 18, with the
    per-frame delay tripled so playback speed is unchanged.
  * Every image is recoloured at build time: pixel luminance is mapped onto the
    KDOS phosphor ramp (dark green to accent green), and the busy shapes (wait,
    progress) ramp to KDOS amber instead, matching the boot splash's
    pending-stage colour. Alpha is un-premultiplied before the mapping and
    re-premultiplied after, so upstream's anti-aliasing survives intact.
  * Alias groups are re-rooted on their CSS names: the real file is `default`
    and `left_ptr` is a symlink to it, not the other way round.

Shapes, hotspots and the remaining animation frames are upstream's work,
unchanged. Both scripts performing the above are distributed alongside this
notice in src/packages/kdos-cursors/.
